<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto I, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1117–1183</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> of Wittelsbach was a Bavarian count palatine and a loyal follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, whom he served on campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. When Barbarossa deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> in 1180, he gave the reduced Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> to Otto, founding the rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">House of Wittelsbach</a>, which lasted in Bavaria until 1918. Otto died in 1183.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Otto I, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown creatorUnknown creator · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_Magnus_Wittelspach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
